concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-19-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19(3) Membership of Council"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-19-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Premier of a State or the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory nominates a person for appointment to the Council, the Minister shall appoint that person as one of the members referred to in paragraph (1)(c) unless the Council already includes a member appointed on the nomination of the Premier of that State or the Chief Minister of that Territory, as the case may be." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If the Premier of a State or the Chief Minister of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory nominates a person for appointment to the Council, the Minister shall appoint that person as one of the members referred to in paragraph (1)(c) unless the Council already includes a member appointed on the nomination of the Premier of that State or the Chief Minister of that Territory, as the case may be."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "13d3eead4bc942b2826ccc9d1c700f9fbee766972de76f2240b40c7ad0fce283" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-19 ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister must appoint a person nominated by the Premier or Chief Minister." ;
